            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to hug, then the Persian for to caress."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ارث بردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ارث بردن (ers bordan) — \"to inherit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او این خانه را از پدربزرگش ارث برد. u in khâne râ az pedarbozorgash ers bord. He inherited this house from his grandfather."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ers 'inheritance' + bordan 'to carry off'; present stem bar-. The giver takes az."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ers is a loan, usually traced to the Arabic word for 'inheritance'; EtymDB has no entry for it. bordan, 'to carry', is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
